    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n`vim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove()` does not work when passing a list of flags.\n\nPassing the flags individually works as expected.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\nCreate minimal.lua:\n\n```lua\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions = \"jcroql\"\n\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove({ \"c\", \"r\", \"o\" })\n\nprint(vim.inspect(vim.opt_local.formatoptions:get()))\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n`nvim --clean -u minimal.lua`\n\nThe resulting formatoptions still contains `c`, `r`, and `o`.\n\nCalling `remove()` separately for each flag works:\n\n```lua\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions = \"jcroql\"\n\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove(\"c\")\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove(\"r\")\nvim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove(\"o\")\n\nprint(vim.inspect(vim.opt_local.formatoptions:get()))\n```\n\nThis correctly removes the three flags.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1644+gaed60b8a53\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWSL\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWin Terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nunrelated\n\n### Installation\n\nfrom repo",
